 County; Central and South Weld County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.56f07ccd30017f7a70b6a91ef8df2e38a8814570.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.56f07ccd30017f7a70b6a91ef8df2e38a8814570.001.1"},{"event":"Air Quality Alert","headline":"Air Quality Alert issued August 27 at 4:10PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"The Colorado Department of Public Health and Environment has\nissued the following...\n\nWHAT...Ozone Action Day Alert.\n\nWHERE...Douglas, Jefferson, Denver, western Arapahoe, western\nAdams, Broomfield, Boulder, Larimer, and Weld Counties\n\nWHEN...400 PM Thursday August 27 to 400 PM Friday August 28\n\nIMPACTS...Ozone Action Day Alert is now in effect for the Front\nRange Urban Corridor.  Hot and sunny weather with scattered\nafternoon storms may allow ozone to reach the Unhealthy for\nSensitive Groups category in western portions of the Denver Metro\narea on Thursday and Friday. For Colorado air quality conditions,\nforecasts, and advisories, visit:\nhttps://www.colorado.gov/airquality/colorado_summary.aspx   If\npossible, please help us reduce ozone pollution by limiting\ndriving gas and diesel-powered vehicles until at least 4 p.m.\nFriday, August 28, 2026. Colorado is also addressing ozone\npollution through state policies. For more information about\nhealth impacts and how ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone- pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-28T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Broomfield, CO; Jefferson, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Adams, CO; Boulder, CO; Weld, CO; Larimer, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a17a27b506afd523954d57cd2deb7b4d9d4ce26d.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a17a27b506afd523954d57cd2deb7b4d9d4ce26d.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-28T19:30:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 281930 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 130 PM MDT Fri Aug 28 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Isolated/scattered high based showers/storms this afternoon/evening with gusty winds. - Temperatures return to the 90s today and Saturday across the plains. - Thunderstorm coverage increases for late Saturday through Monday. && .DISCUSSION /Through Friday/","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-28T19:52:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Saturday... Above-normal temperatures are expected today and Saturday, with scattered high-based showers and storms capable of producing gusty outflows/microbursts each afternoon. Flow aloft is expected to bring some gusty winds (25-30 mph) into North Park both days that will lead to elevated fire weather conditions, but RH is expected to remain above critical t","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"gby01","station_name":"Granby","distance_km":35.3,"soil_temp_5cm_f":81.23,"soil_temp_15cm_f":64.24,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":296.17,"wind_speed_mph":5.59,"air_temp_f":76.68,"relative_humidity":0.24,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/gby01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KBDU","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KBDU 282135Z AUTO 04010G15KT 10SM CLR 33/04 A3008 RMK AO2","temp_f":91,"wind_dir":40,"wind_kt":10,"gust_kt":15,"visibility":"10+","cover":"CLR","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1018.7,"observed":1787952900,"raw_taf":null,"url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KBDU&hours=0"},"airgradien